<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-b7aebeb4bfd946bb88e8dca771b7e90a" title="Practice It!: Cathartic Q2" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false"><qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"><qti-correct-response><qti-value>A</qti-value></qti-correct-response></qti-response-declaration><qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration><qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration><qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Choose the word that best completes the sentence.</p><p>Smashing the last of the broken pottery in the backyard turned out to be strangely ____: all the grief she had bottled up for months came pouring out at once.</p><qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1"><qti-simple-choice identifier="A">cathartic</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">soothing</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">exhilarating</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">nostalgic</qti-simple-choice></qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="CORRECT" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Cathartic means providing emotional release, especially by letting out feelings that have been held in, which is exactly grief 'pouring out at once.' Soothing describes a gentle calming effect rather than a sudden release; exhilarating describes thrilling excitement; and nostalgic describes fond longing for the past.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="INCORRECT" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Bottled-up grief finally pouring out makes the experience cathartic -- it releases pent-up emotion. Soothing means gently calming, which hardly describes smashing pottery; exhilarating means thrilling and energizing; and nostalgic means wistfully remembering the past, a different feeling altogether.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body><qti-response-processing><qti-response-condition><qti-response-if><qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-correct identifier="RESPONSE"/></qti-match><qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE"><qti-base-value base-type="float">1</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value><qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">CORRECT</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">completed</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">hidden</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value></qti-response-if><qti-response-else><qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE"><qti-base-value base-type="float">0</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value><qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">INCORRECT</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">incomplete</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value></qti-response-else></qti-response-condition></qti-response-processing></qti-assessment-item>